<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
%# Shared chrome from homelab-webtheme: theme.css / fonts / favicon come from
%# static.mailmasker.org, so this page restyles with the rest of the fleet and
%# needs no rebuild for a colour change.
%#
%# Shared THEME and FOOTER but NOT the shared HEADER. This page is seen by
%# someone who does not have an account yet -- a top bar with an account
%# dropdown would be nonsense here. The logo carries the identity, same
%# treatment the sso/drive/myaccount sign-in pages get.
%#
%# These templates replace HTML that used to be built with qq{} inside the
%# controller, which is why this package had no templates dir at all until
%# 2026-10-27.
%= include 'homelab/head'
<title><%= title %></title>
<style>
  body {
    margin: 0; min-height: 100vh; display: flex; flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: var(--space-6);
    padding: var(--space-4); background: var(--black-primary);
  }
  .card {
    width: 100%; max-width: 30em; background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-lg); padding: var(--space-8) var(--space-6);
  }
  .brand { text-align: center; margin-bottom: var(--space-6); }
  .brand img { height: 30px; width: auto; }
  h1 {
    font-size: var(--app-xl); font-weight: var(--weight-light);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-tight); margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
  }
  p { font-size: var(--app-base); color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: var(--leading-normal); }

  label {
    display: block; font-weight: var(--weight-medium); font-size: var(--app-sm);
    color: var(--text-secondary); margin: var(--space-4) 0 var(--space-1);
  }
  input {
    width: 100%; padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-3); box-sizing: border-box;
    background: var(--black-secondary); color: var(--text-primary);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-strong); border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    font: inherit; font-size: var(--app-base);
  }
  input::placeholder { color: var(--text-muted); }
  input:hover { border-color: var(--silver-dim); }
  /* Pointer focus gets the same visible ring as keyboard focus -- on a form
     where you are typing a password twice, you should always be able to see
     which field you are in. */
  input:focus { outline: 2px solid var(--focus-ring); outline-offset: 2px; border-color: var(--silver-medium); }

  /* The username field and its fixed "@domain" suffix read as one control. */
  .uname-row { display: flex; align-items: stretch; }
  .uname-row input { border-top-right-radius: 0; border-bottom-right-radius: 0; }
  .uname-suffix {
    display: flex; align-items: center; padding: 0 var(--space-3);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-strong); border-left: 0;
    border-top-right-radius: var(--radius-md); border-bottom-right-radius: var(--radius-md);
    background: var(--surface-hover); color: var(--text-muted); white-space: nowrap;
    font-size: var(--app-base);
  }

  button {
    margin-top: var(--space-6); padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-6);
    border: 1px solid var(--silver-bright); border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    background: var(--silver-bright); color: var(--black-primary);
    font: inherit; font-size: var(--app-base); font-weight: var(--weight-medium);
    cursor: pointer; transition: background var(--transition-fast);
  }
  button:hover { background: #ffffff; }

  /* Suggested-username chips. */
  .chip {
    display: inline-block; margin: var(--space-1) var(--space-1) var(--space-1) 0;
    padding: 0.3em 0.7em; border: 1px solid var(--silver-dim);
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill); background: var(--surface-hover);
    color: var(--silver-bright); cursor: pointer; font-size: var(--app-sm);
  }
  .chip:hover { border-color: var(--silver-medium); background: var(--black-tertiary); }

  .hint { font-size: var(--app-xs); color: var(--text-muted); margin: var(--space-1) 0 0; }
  .msg {
    font-style: italic; color: var(--text-secondary);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--border-strong); padding-left: var(--space-3); margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
  }
  .err { color: var(--error); margin-top: var(--space-4); }
  .ok  { color: var(--success); }
  .appfoot { border: 0; padding: 0; text-align: center; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="card">
  <div class="brand">
    <img src="<%= theme_base %>/logo.svg" alt="Silver Linings">
  </div>
  %# Replaced wholesale by the acceptance page's JS on success, so the card
  %# chrome and the footer below survive it -- the old code overwrote
  %# document.body and took the whole page's styling with it.
  <div id="card-body"><%= content %></div>
</div>
%= include 'homelab/footer'
</body>
</html>
